comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-08T18:17:51.770Z","harness:claude-code","Scope note from the CodeRabbit review of PR 1688. runAction with output_include at the top level and note-edit arguments in options drops the top-level control before validateReadOutputOptions runs. The edit is then written without the read_output_mutation_conflict refusal, and the control is ignored, never applied. This is the same declared-flat-parameter class as pm_history's flat limit; the generic parity harness this item specifies should cover the universal output controls too."
body: ""
